  'Sworn Statement for the Transfer of a Used Vehicle (Ministry of Finance, retail sales tax): the recipient and the donor swear that the transfer is tax exempt. It is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person; the form has no signature fields. Left blank on purpose: the county or regional municipality boxes and the City or Town words (they depend on the address), the acquisition date and the reasons (the owner writes them), and the commissioner block (sworn in person). Draft mapping from the official PDF (https://forms.mgcs.gov.on.ca/dataset/64812fe6-775c-4fbd-98c9-bc9a1c6b1a38/resource/f165f763-c47f-4024-9b16-da60f741e79e/download/1155e.pdf, SHA-256 a2f38dc0ca7ea9b3b9c2369af7b21d6b4694241f1d5eb42b889559246166eb5b; template 05166d7378d9064fba9a0b44c0dc25ef4c0fbde2ac47a3765fb8d0c57ad1b2d5); check every field before use.');
